{
  "name": "LEARN — Validator Output",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "description": "Captures lessons from Validator stage outputs into the Shared Brain (lessons_learned.md only).",
  "when": {
    "type": "fileCreated",
    "patterns": ["**/2_Validator/FINAL_TEST_CASES*.md"]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "LEARN phase (lightweight) — Validator output.\n\nA new Validator file has been created. Your job is to check if it contains any knowledge worth saving to the Shared Brain.\n\nRead the newly created file. Look only for the following — do not invent findings:\n- Non-obvious decisions about tagging test cases as automation vs. regression and why\n- Test coverage patterns that span multiple modules in a non-obvious way\n- Edge cases or scenarios that were difficult to standardise into test cases\n\nFor each genuine finding:\n1. Open .kiro/memory/products/pos/lessons_learned.md and scan for a similar existing entry. If a similar entry already exists, skip this finding entirely.\n2. If the finding is genuinely new, append one line to lessons_learned.md using this exact format:\n   [DATE] [TICKET-ID] [LOGGED] [AUTO] — {concise lesson in one sentence}\n\nRules:\n- Do NOT evaluate any finding for promotion to product.md\n- Do NOT modify pattern_registry.md\n- Do NOT modify project_context.md\n- Do NOT rewrite or edit existing entries\n- If nothing new is found, do nothing and do not write anything"
  }
}
